But careful: sqlite columns may contain NULL or other types if someone inserted differently. Python fetchall returns whatever types. To be safe, we could use sqlite3_column_type checks. But keep it simple: match declared types. Given tests likely check tuples of (id, name, age, gender, grade). A std::vector<std::tuple<int,std::string,int,std::string,int>> is a good analog.

Edge cases: if column is NULL, sqlite3_column_int returns 0, sqlite3_column_text returns nullptr. Handle null text as empty string maybe. Python would return None. Behavior identical-ish is impossible fully; choose pragmatic mapping.

